From 92a0c7ed4e2f07786341640c7358b93b36017612 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:19:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] shader precache: keep the progress of a precache that
 is skipped or stopped

The boot precache builds the game's compute programs only to fill the GPU driver's cache, and
a marker that skips it next time was written only when it ran to the end. Skipped with "Start
now" or ended with the game, its work was forgotten: on an RTX 4060 every boot of Ocarina of
Time again had "4671 of 4794 compute programs to build" (512.8 s the first time, 81.9 s the
next with the driver cache warm), even though 4141 and then 4250 had been built.

The programs built are now recorded next to the precache file (.partial), for the same stamp
as the marker (contents, driver, device, cache version, variant), every 20 s and when the
precache ends unfinished; the next boot leaves them out and builds only the rest. A finished
precache removes the file; a different stamp or a damaged file is ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7yw1ZJY9GYi2KYHfiXxvY
