+/// Progress of a precache that did not run to the end (NEXUS): the compute programs it built,
+/// for the same stamp as a marker (extension .partial). Skipping the precache ("Start now") or
+/// closing the game during it no longer throws its work away: the next boot builds only what is
+/// left. The programs are built to fill the GPU driver's own cache, like the whole precache, so a
+/// program in the list is in that cache exactly as much as one covered by a finished marker.
+std::filesystem::path WarmProgressPath(const std::filesystem::path& warm_file);
+
+/// The built programs (ComputePipelineCacheKey hashes) recorded for `current`; empty when there is
+/// no progress file or it was written for other contents, driver, device, cache version or variant.
+std::unordered_set<u64> ReadWarmProgress(const std::filesystem::path& warm_file,
+                                         const WarmStamp& current);
+
+/// Writes the progress of `warm_file` (replacing the file in one step). False when it cannot.
+bool WriteWarmProgress(const std::filesystem::path& warm_file, const WarmStamp& stamp,
+                       const std::vector<u64>& built);
